## 📄 File-by-File Breakdown

### 1. Python Backends (AI Engines)

#### 🤖 `AIBuddyMode/` (Adaptive AI Buddy Backend)
* [`api.py`](file:///d:/Projects/AI_interview/AIBuddyMode/api.py): FastAPI app running on port `8001`. Handles starting adaptive interviews (`/interview/start`), processing answers (`/interview/answer`), and ending sessions. Saves dynamic state in Redis.
* [`logic.py`](file:///d:/Projects/AI_interview/AIBuddyMode/logic.py): Picks the next question based on whether the candidate answered correctly, targets weak areas, and controls dynamic difficulty levels.
* [`evaluator.py`](file:///d:/Projects/AI_interview/AIBuddyMode/evaluator.py): Formulates system prompts to evaluate correctness, efficiency, and confidence of candidate answers.
* [`state.py`](file:///d:/Projects/AI_interview/AIBuddyMode/state.py): Holds Pydantic models (like `InterviewState` and `WeakArea`) that define the data schema stored in Redis.

#### 📄 `ResumeInterview/` (Resume Analysis Backend)
* [`api.py`](file:///d:/Projects/AI_interview/ResumeInterview/api.py): FastAPI server running on port `8000` to process PDF uploads and parse details.
* [`resumeAnalyzer.py`](file:///d:/Projects/AI_interview/ResumeInterview/resumeAnalyzer.py): Uses RAG (Retrieval-Augmented Generation) to match user resumes with job descriptions, extracting key skills, weaknesses, and experience.

---

### 2. Next.js Frontend Framework (`app/`)

* [`(root)/layout.jsx`](file:///d:/Projects/AI_interview/app/\(root\)/layout.jsx): Renders the main interface layout wrapper containing the responsive navigation sidebar. Skip sidebar logic for buddy mode screens to preserve full-screen layout.
* [`(root)/dashboard/page.jsx`](file:///d:/Projects/AI_interview/app/\(root\)/dashboard/page.jsx): Dashboard landing page displaying analytics, charts (like score progression), and user stats.
* [`(root)/interview/page.jsx`](file:///d:/Projects/AI_interview/app/\(root\)/interview/page.jsx): Mock interview set up panel (difficulty selector, role input) and user's past interview list cards.
* [`(root)/interview/buddy/[inviteCode]/page.jsx`](file:///d:/Projects/AI_interview/app/\(root\)/interview/buddy/\[inviteCode\]/page.jsx): Real-time collaborative interview room with coding editor, shared whiteboard drawing canvas, and chat.

---

### 3. Server Actions & Services (`lib/`)

* [`actions/auth.action.js`](file:///d:/Projects/AI_interview/lib/actions/auth.action.js): Backend server action code for checking logins, credentials matching, cookies verification, email password resetting, and OTP triggers.
* [`actions/general.action.js`](file:///d:/Projects/AI_interview/lib/actions/general.action.js): Core actions for fetching mock interview lists, storing final feedback reports, and caching static interview questions.
* [`security/transaction-manager.js`](file:///d:/Projects/AI_interview/lib/security/transaction-manager.js): Prevents race conditions during simultaneous user score increases or room setups by locking operations through Firestore transactions.
* [`security/auth-utils.js`](file:///d:/Projects/AI_interview/lib/security/auth-utils.js): Password hashing utilities (pbkdf2Sync) and memory cache map to store and verify 6-digit verification codes.
* [`ai-provider.js`](file:///d:/Projects/AI_interview/lib/ai-provider.js): Virtual language model client that performs key rotation, checks key health status, and fails over from Gemini to Groq automatically.

---

### 4. Custom Node Servers (`server/`)

* [`buddy-socket-server.js`](file:///d:/Projects/AI_interview/server/buddy-socket-server.js): Runs on port `4002`. Manages real-time WebSockets connections. Synchronizes note pads, whiteboard shapes, dynamic code outputs, and active room participants utilizing a local Redis store.
* [`piston-local-server.js`](file:///d:/Projects/AI_interview/server/piston-local-server.js): Serves as a wrapper API for the local Piston engine to run untrusted candidate code (C++, Python, JS, Java) securely.
